<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>W-9S Request</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
  .line { border-bottom: 1px solid #000; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .form-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px; }
  .form-group { flex: 1; }
  .full-width { width: 100%; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <h1>CLARK UNIVERSITY SUBSTITUTE FORM W-9S – REQUEST FOR STUDENT'S TAXPAYER IDENTIFICATION NUMBER</h1>

  <p>Clark University ID#: <span data-field="university_id">{{ university_id }}</span></p>

  <p>Name: Please print name as it currently appears on your Clark University ID.</p>

  <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-group">Last Name</div>
    <div class="form-group">First Name</div>
    <div class="form-group">Middle Name/Initial</div>
  </div>

  <p>If the name above is different than the name used by the Social Security Administration or the Internal Revenue please provide that information:</p>

  <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-group">Last Name</div>
    <div class="form-group">First Name</div>
    <div class="form-group">Middle Name/Initial</div>
  </div>

  <p>Permanent Address:</p>
  <div class="line full-width" data-field="permanent_address">{{ permanent_address }}</div>

  <p>Social Security Number or Individual Tax Identification Number:</p>
  <div style="display: flex; gap: 5px;">
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
    <div style="width: 10%;">____</div>
  </div>

  <p>I certify that the number shown on this form is my correct US taxpayer identification number</p>

  <p>Or</p>
  <div style="margin-left: 20px;">
    <input type="checkbox"> I am a foreign national/nonresident alien and do not have a Social Security number or individual taxpayer identification number. I do not plan to file an income tax return in the U.S.
  </div>

  <p>Or</p>
  <div style="margin-left: 20px;">
    <input type="checkbox"> I do not wish to provide my taxpayer identification number to Clark University at this time. I understand that I may be subject to an IRS fine of $50 for failure to do so. I further understand that the IRS will not be able to use the Form 1098-T filed by Clark University to confirm my eligibility for certain education tax benefits without my taxpayer identification number.
  </div>

  <p>Signature:</p>
  <p>Please sign below to authorize Clark University to store this information for internal use and reporting to the IRS. I understand that it will not be used as a public identifier.</p>

  <div class="form-row" style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <div class="form-group">Signature of Student</div>
    <div class="form-group">Date</div>
  </div>

  <p>SEE INSTRUCTIONS ON THE BACK</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>The University requires your correct TIN to file certain information returns with the IRS and to provide you a Form 1098-T, Tuition Statement. For students, this will be your social security number (SSN) or, if you are not eligible to obtain an SSN, your individual taxpayer identification number (ITIN). Please note that if you are a non-resident alien and do not have income that is subject to tax, you are not required to supply this information and you should indicate this by checking the appropriate box on the Substitute Form W-9S.</p>

  <p>Form 1098-T contains information about payments made for tuition and other related expenses to help determine whether you, or the person who can claim you as a dependent, may take either the tuition and fees deduction or claim a deduction credit to reduce Federal income tax. For more information, see IRS Publication 970, Tax Benefits for Higher Education. Under US Federal law, you are required to provide the requested information.</p>

  <h2>Penalties</h2>
  <p>Under Federal law, you are required to provide the requested information. Failure to provide your correct SSN or ITIN to Clark University could result in a penalty of $50.00 to you from the IRS, unless your failure is due to reasonable cause and not willful neglect.</p>

  <h2>Information</h2>
  <p>Your name and mailing address should match that used by the Social Security Administration or Internal Revenue Service.</p>

  <p>If you do not have a SSN or ITIN, you may apply for one and fill out and return this form when you receive it.</p>

  <p>Deliver or mail the completed form to the address below. DO NOT EMAIL the form. Email is not a secure way to transmit personal information.</p>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <strong>Hand Deliver</strong><br>
      Student Accounts Office<br>
      Shaich ASEC Building, 3rd Floor<br>
      939 Main Street<br>
      Worcester, MA 01610
    </div>
    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <strong>Mailing Address</strong><br>
      Clark University<br>
      Attention: Student Accounts<br>
      950 Main Street<br>
      Worcester MA 01610
    </div>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top: 50px;">Do not submit this form to the IRS</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>